The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object, whose documented rule says 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text', returns the same answer for two replies that the rule requires it to tell apart: for Reply A (````
{"a": 1}
````
{"b": 2}) it returns {"b": 2} instead of the required {"a": 1}, and for Reply B ({"a": 1}
{"b": 2}) it returns {"b": 2} as required, because the function only recognizes three-backtick fences and treats the four-backtick fence in Reply A as ordinary text.